  "comments": {
    "q10-A": "hmm, the page after should take effect even if we navigate",
    "q15-A": "This should be something tunable at the app level, e.g. so I can say/do something different, or have the auth logic defined once.\n\n`when any server call fails\n    if the error is \"not authorized\"\n       show the login page\n       return\n`\nSo app logic can skip the auth check.\n\nIf I don't want the default error notice to show up, I can put an `otherwise do nothing` in there",
    "q2-A": "if they want to make sure they always have a fresh copy, they can load it explicitly",
    "q7-A": "both `if completing...` and `when completing...`",
    "q8-A": "In the netbox api page, `the server` should be an alias for `netbox`\ne.g. `netbox is a web server` => implies that the base class for netbox is `web server` whose base class is `server`.\n\n`call netbox` should work as well\n\nNot sure if files (CSV etc) should have special syntax for now, let's assume they are \"call the server\" for now.",
    "q9-B": "A page is part of an app.\nI'd be OK defining page/app files as `foo.page.spell` and `foo.app.spell` if it makes things easier"
  },
